{"provider": "mdn", "capability": "page", "recorded_at": "2026-11-13T09:12:19+00:00", "params": {"path": "Web/API/Response/json"}, "expected_records": 1, "body": {"doc": {"body": [{"type": "prose", "value": {"id": null, "title": null, "isH3": false, "content": "<div class=\"notecard note\"><p><strong>Note:</strong> This feature is available in <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Workers_API\">Web Workers</a>.</p></div>\n<p>The <strong><code>json()</code></strong> method of the <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Response\"><code>Response</code></a> interface takes\na <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Response\"><code>Response</code></a> stream and reads it to completion. It returns a promise which\nresolves with the result of parsing the body text as <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON\"><code>JSON</code></a>.</p>\n<p>Note that despite the method being named <code>json()</code>, the result is not JSON but is instead the result of taking JSON as input and parsing it to produce a JavaScript object.</p>"}}, {"type": "prose", "value": {"id": "syntax", "title": "Syntax", "isH3": false, "content": "<div class=\"code-example\"><div class=\"example-header\"><span class=\"language-name\">js</span></div><pre class=\"brush: js notranslate\"><code>json()\n</code></pre></div>"}}, {"type": "prose", "value": {"id": "parameters", "title": "Parameters", "isH3": true, "content": "<p>None.</p>"}}, {"type": "prose", "value": {"id": "return_value", "title": "Return value", "isH3": true, "content": "<p>A <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Promise\"><code>Promise</code></a> that resolves to a JavaScript object. This object could be\nanything that can be represented by JSON — an object, an array, a string, a number…</p>"}}, {"type": "prose", "value": {"id": "exceptions", "title": "Exceptions", "isH3": true, "content": "<dl>\n<dt id=\"aborterror\"><code>AbortError</code> <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/DOMException\"><code>DOMException</code></a></dt>\n<dd>\n<p>The request was <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Fetch_API/Using_Fetch#canceling_a_request\">aborted</a>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt id=\"typeerror\"><a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/TypeError\"><code>TypeError</code></a></dt>\n<dd>\n<p>Thrown for one of the following reasons:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The response body is <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Fetch_API/Using_Fetch#locked_and_disturbed_streams\">disturbed or locked</a>.</li>\n<li>There was an error decoding the body content (for example, because the <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Encoding\"><code>Content-Encoding</code></a> header is incorrect).</li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt id=\"syntaxerror\"><a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/SyntaxError\"><code>SyntaxError</code></a></dt>\n<dd>\n<p>The response body cannot be parsed as JSON.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>"}}, {"type": "prose", "value": {"id": "examples", "title": "Examples", "isH3": false, "content": "<p>In our <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/dom-examples/tree/main/fetch/fetch-json\" class=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"External link (opens in new tab)\">fetch JSON example</a> (run <a href=\"https://mdn.github.io/dom-examples/fetch/fetch-json/\" class=\"external\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"External link (opens in new tab)\">fetch JSON live</a>),\nwe create a new request using the <a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Request/Request\" title=\"Request()\"><code>Request()</code></a> constructor, then use it to fetch a <code>.json</code> file.\nWhen the fetch is successful, we read and parse the data using <code>json()</code>, then read\nvalues out of the resulting objects as you'd expect and insert them into list items to\ndisplay our product data.</p>\n<div class=\"code-example\"><div class=\"example-header\"><span class=\"language-name\">js</span></div><pre class=\"brush: js notranslate\"><code>const myList = document.querySelector(\"ul\");\nconst myRequest = new Request(\"products.json\");\n\nfetch(myRequest)\n  .then((response) =&gt; response.json())\n  .then((data) =&gt; {\n    for (const product of data.products) {\n      const listItem = document.createElement(\"li\");\n      listItem.appendChild(document.createElement(\"strong\")).textContent =\n        product.Name;\n      listItem.append(` can be found in ${product.Location}. Cost: `);\n      listItem.appendChild(document.createElement(\"strong\")).textContent =\n        `£${product.Price}`;\n      myList.appendChild(listItem);\n    }\n  })\n  .catch(console.error);\n</code></pre></div>"}}, {"type": "specifications", "value": {"id": "specifications", "title": "Specifications", "isH3": false, "specifications": [{"bcdSpecificationURL": "https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#ref-for-dom-body-json①", "title": "Fetch"}], "query": "api.Response.json"}}, {"type": "browser_compatibility", "value": {"id": "browser_compatibility", "title": "Browser compatibility", "isH3": false, "query": "api.Response.json"}}, {"type": "prose", "value": {"id": "see_also", "title": "See also", "isH3": false, "content": "<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/API/Service_Worker_API\">ServiceWorker API</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CORS\">Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP\">HTTP</a></li>\n</ul>"}}], "isActive": true, "isMarkdown": true, "isTranslated": false, "locale": "en-US", "mdn_url": "/en-US/docs/Web/API/Response/json", "modified": "2025-08-19T19:45:56.000Z", "native": "English (US)", "noIndexing": false, "other_translations": [{"locale": "en-US", "title": "Response: json() method", "native": "English (US)"}, {"locale": "de", "title": "Response: Methode json()", "native": "Deutsch"}, {"locale": "fr", "title": "Response : méthode json()", "native": "Français"}, {"locale": "ja", "title": "Response: json() メソッド", "native": "日本語"}, {"locale": "ko", "title": "Response: json() 메서드", "native": "한국어"}, {"locale": "zh-CN", "title": "Response：json() 方法", "native": "中文 (简体)"}], "p